DESCRIPTION:If you are a newcomer to Canada and want to enhance your Engli
 sh communication skills\, this free program is for you! Please note\, this
  is an opportunity to practice your conversational skills—it is not a f
 ormal English class.\nThis program is in partnership with WoodGreen Commun
 ity Services.\nAfter registering online\, you will be contacted by WoodGre
 en staff to complete your registration.\nPlease be aware that this program
  will be taking a break in December.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe 
 personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Libra
 ry under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). Th
 e information will only be used for event and program registration\, deliv
 ery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your informati
 on can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5
 981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Pape/Danforth\, Second floor program room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a501360fb418a280099d5c0
X-SOURCE:Volunteer Toronto
END:VEVENT
