BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Citizenship Education Circle with CultureLink
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261117T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261117T203000
UID:6aa08a274995480655ee01e6@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:CultureLink offers a 10 week session to prepare for the Citize
 nship test. Attend every week to improve your skills.\n- Learn about the t
 est's content and structure\n- Get support and tips from our Volunteer Men
 tors\n- Practice with sample quizzes\nFunded by Immigration\, Refugees and
  Citizenship Canada in Partnership with Toronto Public Library.\nInformati
 on Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected 
 by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20
 (a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and p
 rogram registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the lib
 rary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nansw
 erline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, 3rd floor\, Discussion Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa08a274995480655ee01e6
X-SOURCE:Volunteer Toronto
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Building Your Personal & Business Brand
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261118T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261118T160000
UID:6a9ae03ebe148200298c77e9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This introductory workshop helps participants understand and m
 anage their personal brand in alignment with their professional goals. It
  covers key business branding elements and offers actionable steps to enh
 ance brand presence. Through interactive activities\, participants will a
 pply what they’ve learned to develop both personal and business brands\
 , while exploring marketing strategies and campaign elements.\nInformatio
 n Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected b
 y the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(
 a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and pr
 ogram registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the libr
 ary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswe
 rline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Maria A. Shchuka\, 1st floor the Children's Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9ae03ebe148200298c77e9
X-SOURCE:Volunteer Toronto
END:VEVENT
